===Etymology 2===
From an earlier {{m|de|Munt}}, from {{inh|de|gem-pro|*mundō}}. The retention of /d/ in the combination /nd/ is a signature of northern [[High German]] dialects and only becomes widespread after a period in the Middle Ages where the southern [[reflex]] /nt/ is favoured in southern writings.

====Noun====
{{de-noun|f|Mund|Munde}}

# {{senseid|de|hand}} {{lb|de|obsolete}} [[hand]]
# {{lb|de|obsolete}} [[legal]] [[protection]]

=====Usage notes=====
* Due to [[conflation]] with the masculine noun, combined nouns based on this one are also masculine.

